anization was established in response to the growing awareness of the limitations of the Earth’s resources, particularly in the context of rapid population growth and industrialization. Its significance lies in its role as a catalyst for both scholarly discourse and public policy concerning sustainable development and global governance, marking a shift in the way societies address complex interdependencies in the modern world.

